  "benchmark": "A frozen learned policy plays at least 100,000 fresh 200bb HUNL Slumbot hands, scores above 0 bb/100, and has a 95% confidence-interval lower bound above 0.",
  "hypothesis": "At the previously validated finite-update dose of 5e-5 parent KL, adding both public-opponent seat objectives through normalized MGDA will improve all nine frozen-cohort objectives in both independent 1M lineages, outperform the matched seven-objective control on both public seats, and preserve rather than trade away untouched learned-anchor breadth.",
  "material_change": "From each retained 1M parent and the immutable public-objective audit cohort, create matched resume-ineligible seven-objective control and nine-objective treatment checkpoints calibrated to exactly 5e-5 parent KL. First require finite-step improvement of intended objectives in both lineages and a better public-seat loss change for treatment. Only on pass, run untouched common-deck greedy evaluation across Standard10, CFR4, legacy_iter16, and legacy_mixed65k for both lineages, plus a separate fresh public-opponent two-seat comparison. This is a bounded translation test, not environment training.",
  "baseline": "Seven-objective 5e-5 update previously translated to +1.0361 +/-2.6417 bb/100 pooled but was negative on Standard10 and one lineage. Naive 25%-public PPO was significantly worse than control. The new frozen nine-objective geometry passed both lineages and all 8/8 folds.",
  "source": "v6-integrated-public-objective-gradient-feasibility-20260903 immutable raw cohort and gradients; retained seed1/seed2 1M parents; Standard10 source.",
  "parent_id": "v6-integrated-public-objective-gradient-feasibility-20260903",
