  "notes": [
    "Preregistered interpretation: finite-step failure rejects only this dose and triggers a lower-dose boundary check. Offline success admits untouched evaluation; external failure rejects promotion but does not reject long-horizon conflict-aware learning unless the mechanism itself reverses.",
    "At matched 5e-5 parent KL, both arms improved every reward group in Seed1 but crossed the nonlinear source-KL basin; nine-treatment source KL increased by 6.47e-6 and seven-control by 7.87e-6. Seed2 nine-treatment improved all nine. Per preregistration, no untouched evaluation was run; continue same frozen cohort at a fourfold lower dose.",
    "At 1.25e-5 parent KL, both seven-control and nine-treatment improve their intended finite objectives in both lineages; nine-treatment improves all nine and beats control on both public-seat losses in each lineage. The preregistered untouched-evaluation gate passed.",
    "Seed1 untouched learned-anchor panel is directionally negative but statistically inconclusive: -0.1587 +/-0.2881 bb/100; 1/4 anchors positive, seat0 +0.0977 and seat1 -0.4150. Run the preregistered independent Seed2 panel before interpretation.",
    "Seed2 independently repeats the breadth sign pattern: nine-minus-seven negative pooled and on Standard10, legacy_iter16, and legacy_mixed65k; only CFR4 positive. Its pooled estimate -1.6113 +/-2.7403 crosses zero because rare greedy divergences against mixed65k are high variance. Run fresh public-opponent paired evaluation to distinguish target translation from broad tradeoff.",
    "Seed1 nine-treatment translates directionally on fresh public-opponent deals: +0.2686 bb/100 versus seven-control, CI [-0.1403,+0.6774]. Seat0 is exactly unchanged and seat1 +0.5371. This is positive but inconclusive; replicate Seed2.",
    "Seed2 public-opponent target translation is negative and inconclusive at -0.4395 bb/100, CI [-1.3192,+0.4403], so the positive Seed1 target result does not replicate. Aggregate all raw pair evidence and stop promotion.",
    "Canonical alpha_holdem suite passed 329/329. The 5e-5 checkpoints are preserved as dose-boundary evidence and resume-ineligible; 1.25e-5 checkpoints are evaluation-only and not promoted. No environment training or Slumbot hands were generated."
  ],
  "result": {
    "summary": "The nine-objective geometry was locally valid, but its 5e-5 finite step crossed the Seed1 Standard10-KL basin. A fourfold lower 1.25e-5 step improved all nine frozen objectives in both independent lineages and beat the seven-objective control on both frozen public seats. Untouched evaluation then covered 98,304 hands with complete raw-pair/hash integrity.",
    "conclusion": "The public-opponent objective addition does not translate robustly beyond its frozen cohort. Against four learned anchors, nine-minus-seven was -0.8850 bb/100 with 95% CI [-2.2627,+0.4927], negative in both lineages, negative on Standard10/iter16/mixed65k, and positive only on CFR4. Against fresh public-model deals it was -0.0854, CI [-0.5705,+0.3996], with opposite lineage signs. Thus the local common-descent geometry is real but neither target reward nor general breadth replicates. This explicitly rejects promotion of this bounded public-objective intervention; it does not reject long-horizon self-play or league learning for insufficient scale.",
    "decision": "REJECT_PUBLIC_OBJECTIVE_ADDITION_AND_RETAIN_1M_PARENT",
    "next_step": "Do not scale the nine-objective checkpoint or revive naive public-opponent mixing. Reassess the research portfolio using geometric learning curves, multi-seed breadth, Standard10 preservation, and proxy-to-Slumbot alignment. Select a long-horizon learned-weight method only when its mechanism is not contradicted; prioritize objectives whose proxy direction has external support rather than adding another local teacher constraint."
  },
